      en:'Spanish settlers founded the pueblo of “Our Lady Queen of the Angels” in 1781; it became Mexican after independence and American after the Mexican War. Railways, oil and film made Los Angeles explode in the twentieth century, and Hollywood became the world’s film capital. It is also a mirror of race and immigration: the Watts riots of 1965 and the Rodney King riots of 1992 took place here.',
